Deliberately empty, and deliberately committed.

Turning the framework preset off makes Vercel treat this project as a plain
build, so after the build command it looks for a static output directory and
fails the deploy if there isn't one. This API emits no static files — the build
only generates the Prisma client, migrates and seeds — so this directory exists
to be found and left alone. Nothing is ever served from it: the rewrite in
vercel.json sends every path to the function.

See "An empty public/, and why it has to exist" in ../README.md.
